I have got the hang of the game to a point that I can take my Samurai down to
level 25. I usualy DIE there, though, because of a perticulary _nasty_ Medusa.

I always seem to end up on, near, or close to her. And I NEVER CAN KEEP MY
BLINDFOLD PAST lvl 18!

But, I have REFLECTION! yes, boys and ghouls, I manage to (3 out of 10) get my
hands on ether a amulet or shield of reflection.  I have bounced of Pissed off
Deity's bolts with them (But not the Wide Angle Disintergration Beam), but 
never the Medusa's gaze. Why? I can use the shield to bounce ALL the breath 
weapons, rays, bolts, but not one nasty look. I cannot to this with a mirror,
but only a mirror can do this.  Persius did not use a mirror, he used a 
polished *SHIELD*, would it not be a better case to have the following?

D - a +1 shield of reflection (Worn)
The Medusa gazes at you  -more-
She sees her reflection in your shield! -more-
She turns to stone! -more-
Your shield darkens
D - a +1 shield of the Medusa (Worn)
(The shield, now embossed with the Medusa's face, no longer reflects, but does
scare monster)

